# The cable, spelled two ways, as on macie: `cabled-macie` for a person, and
# 10.77.77.1 for anything that has to name the route it took. The reverse
# enrollment needs the addressable spelling for the same reason macie's does
# -- `macie` picks its route by probe and never says which. BindAddress keeps
# it honest: 10.77.77.2 is here only while the cable is. Tight keepalives, as
# in 05-, because ten seconds of silence on a 1.7 ms link means it is gone.

Host cabled-macie 10.77.77.1
    HostName 10.77.77.1
    User fredrir
    HostKeyAlias macie
    BindAddress 10.77.77.2
    ServerAliveInterval 5
    ServerAliveCountMax 2
